  "body": "## What changed\nHovering a selection row in an operation's Geometry tab (its label, its remove button, or anywhere on the row) now lights that face, chain/edge or vertex in the viewport with a strong hover highlight: a 7 px dark halo under a 3.5 px hot-magenta stroke (`Overlay::RowHover`, a dark and a light value), apart from the violet pick, the 1 px yellow viewport hover and the other overlay inks. It clears when the pointer leaves.\n\nRoot cause worth knowing: the old label hover set `State.geo_hover`, but the shell cleared it at frame start and the viewport pane draws before the properties pane sets it, so it never reached the draw (the highlight did not work at all). Fix: `State.geo_hover_drawn` carries last frame's value to the viewport (one-frame lag; a repaint is requested whenever the two differ). The thin `hover_features` pass no longer repeats the row hover; `interact::row_hover_segments` is the strong layer. Ephemeral view state in `State` (the existing hover precedent), no command, no undo, no direct world pokes. Decision: `docs/decisions/1507-geometry-row-hover.md`.\n\nReverse direction (hover in viewport marks the row) is not done: filed as #1519 (P4, effort:medium, area:ui).\n\nOverlap: #1330 and #1314 touch ui files but not the geometry tab or the hover draw; #1505 (edge selected style) is untouched here, the hover ink was chosen distinct from the current pick inks.\n\n## Pins\n- `egui_app::tests::geo_row_hover::hovering_a_selection_row_or_its_remove_button_sets_the_hovered_selection`: face, chain and vertex rows; label and remove-button hover set `geo_hover` to that row's entity, row 2/3 give theirs, leaving clears it and the viewport draw segments, no command filed.\n- `geo_row_hover::row_hover_style_is_strong_and_distinct_in_both_themes`: named constants, ink distinct from the other overlay inks in both themes.\n- `law_tests::preview_tests::hover_features_lights_the_face_boundary` (updated): row hover goes through `row_hover_segments`; stale/gone/hidden draw nothing.\n\nMutation checks (each reverted): drop remove-button/row-rect hover -> row-0 remove-button assertion fails; shell never clears -> \"leaving clears row 0\" fails; `row_hover_segments` empty -> \"reaches the draw list\" fails; 1 px stroke -> style test fails; drop the one-frame carry -> \"reaches the draw list\" fails. Not pinned: reading `geo_hover` instead of `geo_hover_drawn` in the draw is indistinguishable post-frame (the ordering is exercised only by a real two-pane frame; the screenshot shows it works).\n\nGates: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green; `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=1` 710 passed; clippy ui + app `-D warnings` clean. No snapshot PNGs touched.\n\nScreenshots: attached below (headless `harness.render()` of the throwaway test, which was deleted; the render has no GPU mesh, only the egui overlay, hovering the chain row). Local: `~/Desktop/camcraft/builds/pr-1507-hover/before.png` and `after.png` (before = no highlight, which is also what upstream main drew, per the root cause above).\n\nChangelog: | fix(ui): hovering a Geometry-tab selection row or its remove button highlights the pick strongly in the viewport (#1507) |\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1507\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
